    "result_text": "The full suite ran \u2014 `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the project, and it passes. The build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the audit-on-create requirement: on a successful owner create, an audit line is emitted via the logger named `AUDIT` containing the owner id, customerCode, and registrationDate.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **New `OwnerAuditLogger` component** (`service/OwnerAuditLogger.java`) \u2014 a small, single-responsibility Spring `@Component` that owns audit-trail logging for owner lifecycle events. It logs to the dedicated `AUDIT` logger, keeping audit side-effects out of the request-handling and persistence code. Its `logCreated(Owner)` method records the id, customerCode, and registrationDate.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1`** \u2014 injected the new logger and call `ownerAuditLogger.logCreated(owner)` immediately after `saveOwner(owner)` succeeds. This is the point where all three values are populated: the id is assigned by persistence, the customerCode is generated in `saveOwner`, and the registrationDate is set earlier in the create flow.\n\nThe `AUDIT` logger inherits the root `INFO` level from `logback.xml`, so the line propagates to the test's `ListAppender`. The acceptance test (`coreLogsAuditOnCreate`) and the full suite pass.",
